{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults","id":1545774,"title":"[MtAw Dark Eras] Fan created Great Cults","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-12T23:18:16-08:00","id":1545774,"title":"[MtAw Dark Eras] Fan created Great Cults","content":"I remind everyone that <b>Great Cults</b> are 'magical mythos explained' before great unification by Atlantean Orders. Where <b>Darshanas</b> are philosophies WHY we do magic - Great Cults answer HOW we do magic and from WHERE magic comes. In Atlantean Orders Darshanas are general ideas Orders themselves ( warrior, priest &amp; judges, researchers and spies mages ) - where Atlantean Great Cult is '<i>magic comes from Atlantis, wonderous magical island, where dragons were - all of that cause of Supernal Realms incarnating in this particular place as mega Demense'</i>. \ud83d\ude09 [ In 1E <b>Great Cults </b>where called <b>Magical Traditions</b> ( in book of the same name) or <b>Mythos</b> ( in <b>Tome of Mysteries </b>), sorta. ]<br /> <br /> I run now series of historical games, I may need some new Great Cults, not mentioned in official materials for gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-14-2024, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T23:28:13-08:00","id":1545775,"title":"","content":"In coming games I may need Norse/Vikings Great Cult - so here are my first rough drafts of it. I will edit this post with updates on material. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <b><i>Sei\u00f0r</i></b><i> (? Not sure on name )</i><br /> <br /> <b>What is magic? </b>Magic is boon and curse from Gods, both <i>Aesir </i>and <i>Vanir.</i> It was stolen by them from <i>Jotunn</i>, Giants.<br /> <br /> <b>What is Fallen World? </b>World is carcass of great Giant Yamir, killed by first Gods.<br /> <br /> <b>Who are Exarchs and Oracles? </b>Exarchat by Norse are known as <i><b>Giants</b></i>, first evil gods that rules universe. Oracles in that cosmology are Aesir 'good' gods.<br /> <br /> <b>What is Abyss</b>? Abyss is great void of <b>Ginnungagap -</b> non-existence between Nine Worlds themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>What is Supernal Realms? </b>Supernal is called <i><b>Nine Worlds</b></i>, with Midgard ( Earth ) being only one of those relaties. Sei\u00f0r mages think there could more Paths than those typical found. ( General, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1047550-dark-eras-wolf-and-raven-nine-realms\">Fallen Worlds Realms associations are in that topic</a>. ) <br /> <br /> 1. <b>Midgard:</b> The world of humans. The physical/material/Fallen World.<br /> <br /> 2.<b> Jotunheim</b>: Probable Transcendental Realm, ruling over other Supernal, where Oracles and Exarchs origin? ( See <b>Silver Ladder</b> book on that. )<br /> <br /> 3 &amp; 4. <b>Asgard &amp; </b><b>Vanaheim </b>- Primal Wild<br /> <br /> 5 &amp; 6.\u200b<b>Alfheim &amp; Svartalfheim</b>: Arcadia<br /> <br /> 7. <b>Helheim </b>- Stygia<br /> <br /> 8. <b>Muspelheim </b>- Aether<br /> <br /> <b>9. Niflheim</b> - Pandemonium - Norse version of 'Labiyrynthine Realm of remose' is mist bonud icy realm, not in demons and fire.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Yggdrasil </b>is Emanation Realm connecting all the rest of Nine Worlds.<br /> <br /> <b>What are local Darshanas (proto-Orders)?</b><ul><li><b>Bearserke ( Adamantino Velos )</b> - Sacred warriors, touched by Odins mad rage. High in their armies are <i><b>Valkyrie</b></i>, mostly women chosen by gods.</li> <li><b>Brokke</b> (? From <b>Brokkr dwarf - Velos &amp; Ajivaki, </b>future Nameless )<b> - </b>craftsman and servants, they practice magic by serving. <b>Legacies:</b> <i>Forge Masters</i> ( <b>Legacies: The Ancient</b> )\u200b</li> <li><b>Gothi ( Omphalos )</b> - Priest and judges in temples of great Aesir. Each Gothi circle is lead by Hofgothi - high priest. ( SL Deacon equivalent )</li> <li><b>Skaldi ( Gnostikon )</b> - Lore keepers and bards, sustaining lore and telling Sagas of local heroes. <b>Legacies: </b><i>Skalds</i> ( <b>Legacies: The Ancient</b> )</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-13-2024, 05:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T06:21:34-08:00","id":1545783,"title":"","content":"Maybe one made after Aztec mythology. The Watchtowers are each of the 5 suns and magic is drawing upon their power, the Oracles are the gods that embodied those suns. The Abyss is Cipactli, ever spawning horrors to feed its insatiable appetite and break free of its bonds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T13:38:39-08:00","id":1545812,"title":"","content":"Rough draft for <b>Awakened Christianity</b> - for my Rome games. ( It's very important for Rome Empire in 2nd till 5th century AD - and probably from there on. ) Probably similar would work probably for Judaism and Islam versions of it.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Awakened Christianity</i></b><br /> <br /> <b>What is magic? </b>Magic is boon send from God and their angels.<br /> <br /> <b>What is Fallen World? </b>World was created perfect by God. With Atlantean fall of Towers to Heaven - God cursed whole creation to become Fallen World as it is.<br /> <br /> <b>Who are Exarchs and Oracles? </b>Exarch AND Oracles are both emanations of One True God. Many times they are called as Archangels on particular Path.<br /> <br /> <b>What is High Speech</b>? High Speech is language of Angels - later known as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enochian\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Enochian</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>What is Abyss</b>? Absence of the divine light, pointed to the theology of St Augustine of Hippo. Some intellectual in Awakened Christianity posits it's parts of Creation rejected by God. In later centuries other posits it's literal Hell, or spread of Hell, directly from the Devil.<br /> <br /> <b>What is Supernal Realms? </b>Supernal Realms are higher planes, outside of normal reality, each governed by one Archangel. They are still only 'filters' of One True Higher reality, ruled all at once, by God themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Aether</b> - Havens of All Mighty, under <b><i>Archangel Micheal</i></b><br /> <b>Arcadia</b> - Under guidance of <i><b>Gabriel</b></i>, past World BEFORE Creation of Humans - perfect, but also somehow pagan.<br /> <b>Pandemonium</b> - Purgatory, ruled by the angel of judgment <i><b>Phanuel</b></i>. ( In Middle Ages, it's changed into literal 'Hell of sinners, ruled by <i><b>Lucifer</b></i>' )<br /> <b>Primal Wild </b>- Garden of Eden AFTER creation of Adam and Eve, especially with Tree of Knowledge, under guidance of <i><b>Rafael</b></i><br /> <b>Stygia</b> - Mausoleums and Cathedrals of previous dead, under watch of <b><i>Uriel </i></b>( See <a href=\"https://www.angelarium.net/seraphim#/the-driftwood-cathedral/\" target=\"_blank\">Driftwood Cathedral</a> for inspiration )<br /> <br /> <b>What are local Darshanas (proto-Orders)?</b><br /> Christianity was created just AFTER first integration of Atlantean Orders in Ancient Rome, circa 1st century BCE. ( With Christianity creation on whole 1st century AD. ) It's widespread of this religion in Mediterranean Sea area is joined with creation Diamond as organisations Alliance. All of Darshanas of it ARE Atlantean and Seers Orders - even in modern times, it's rather minority percentage but still sustained in general multicultural tapestry of Diamond Cults beliefs systems, when more and more Awakened eshew more religious roots of their magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-16-2024, 05:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T18:50:58-08:00","id":1545826,"title":"","content":"Pandemonium could be Purgatory, ruled by the angel of judgment Phanuel. It would align more with the idea of scouring away your weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Stygia could be the <a href=\"https://www.angelarium.net/seraphim#/the-driftwood-cathedral/\" target=\"_blank\">Driftwood Cathedral</a>. Serene, quiet, where you have time to let go.<br /> <br /> Then make the Primal Wilds into the Ark of the Covenant, hosting every living being that was and could be. <br /> <br /> The Abyss could be the absence of the divine light, if you base it on the theology of St Augustine of Hippo. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-13T21:28:20-08:00","id":1545832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1545826#post1545826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pandemonium could be Purgatory, ruled by the angel of judgment Phanuel. It would align more with the idea of scouring away your weaknesses.<br /> <br /> Stygia could be the <a href=\"https://www.angelarium.net/seraphim#/the-driftwood-cathedral/\" target=\"_blank\">Driftwood Cathedral</a>. Serene, quiet, where you have time to let go.<br /> <br /> Then make the Primal Wilds into the Ark of the Covenant, hosting every living being that was and could be.<br /> <br /> The Abyss could be the absence of the divine light, if you base it on the theology of St Augustine of Hippo.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Really. great ideas, I stole them all! Only Primal Wild and Arcadia I still make Garden of Eden - <b>Ark of Covenant</b> is antithetical to the Primal Wilds main imaginary. Yes, you have all animals in there - but they are all locked up in wood confinement. In Wilds, Beasts are roaming the world, free of limitations.<br /> <br /> I updated <b><i>Awakened Christianity</i></b> post with you ideas and my refinement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T00:33:25-08:00","id":1545835,"title":"","content":"From what we see, I think the Great Cults represent cultures that are stable and homogenous enough that everyone in them can more or less agree on a single cultural cosmology. Whoever you talk to in Greece, they more or less see magic in the same cultural idiom. They're not exclusionary exactly, it's just that there aren't that many people from outside the culture.<br /> <br /> That's why the era of <i>To The Strongest</i> is so important. Large numbers of mages from different Great Cults meet each other and realise that things they though were very important, are indeed simply cultural idioms.<br /> <br /> Christianity by definition doesn't have that. It's surrounded by a pagan culture that has radically different ideas. You can't really be a mage and think only in a Christian idiom, because other mages are blatantly able to interact with the Supernal in the same manner as you without it (I suspect those who can't accept that, go Banisher). It also won't have a consistent cosmology for a long time. I think you'd need to wait till a millennia or so late for Christianity to have that kind of intellectual hegemony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T23:28:56-08:00","id":1545922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1545812#post1545812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rough draft for <b>Awakened Christianity</b> - for my Rome games. ( It's very important for Rome Empire in 2nd till 5th century AD - and probably from there on..) Very similarly would work probably for Judaism and Islam versions of it.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Awakened Christianity</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder how <b>Awakened Islam</b> would differ from Christianity? Beside names of ArchAngels ruling Supernal realms? And maybe different role of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iblis?wprov=sfla1\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Iblis/Devil</b></a> in that cosmology as direct lord of Pandemonium - that is much more accurate in Islam as he is pointed as 'Great Tester' of humanity, not doing 'evil for evil sake only'.<br /> <br /> I remember from <b>Tome of Mysteries</b> implication that in Islam, mages much more rely on High Speech Runes because of '<i>cultural ban on images of humans</i>'. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-15-2024, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T05:54:31-08:00","id":1545929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1545922#post1545922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how <b>Awakened Islam</b> would differ from Christianity? Beside names of ArchAngels ruling Supernal names? And maybe different role of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iblis?wprov=sfla1\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Iblis/Devil</b></a> in that cosmology?</div> </div> </div> </div>Christianity is trinitarian while Islam is strictly monotheistic, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christianity_and_Islam#Similarities_and_differences\" target=\"_blank\">for starters</a>, but as Michael says, a cosmopolitan cultural context is the exact sort of circumstance that caused the Darshanas to emerge and form the Diamond that supplanted the Great Cults, and Islam's foundational prophet was born and died near the end of the Scholastic Age.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I remember from <b>Tome of Mysteries</b> implication that in Islam, mages much more rely on High Speech Runes because of ' <i>cultural ban on images of humans</i>'. \ud83e\udd14 </div> </div> </div>Unless you're referring to some passage that does not use the word &quot;Islam&quot; or Muslim,&quot; there is no such line in Tome of the Mysteries; the only reference TotM makes to Islam is to compare the Palimpsest form of runes/glyphs to Islamic geometric art.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T13:22:41-08:00","id":1545960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1545922#post1545922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how <b>Awakened Islam</b> would differ from Christianity?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a dark era on Storyteller Vault called <i>The Goal of the Wise</i> that covers Andalusia from 912-976CE. It seems like a pretty decent attempt to merge Awakening with medieval Islamic cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T19:33:01-08:00","id":1545981,"title":"","content":"So I can simplify the &quot;Christian Great Cult&quot; and &quot;Islamic Great Cult&quot; real nice and simple: there never would have been any; there would be, at best, Nameless Orders and Legacies.<br /> <br /> The Synhedrion aren't described in great detail in the Tome of the Pentacle, but between the fact that their one major entry implies that all theorizing about one Yeshua ben Yosef was provided to the Diamond by the Synhedrion and the way Dave frames it when he talks about them (I will namely highlight <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511880-tome-of-the-pentacle-on-dtrpg?p=1513112#post1513112\">&quot;If every Great Cult provided something to the melting pot of the Diamond, their main contribution was a sense of responsibility.&quot;</a>), the Judean Great Cult was pretty well in the mix* by the time the Diamond officially forms by the Alexandrian Convocation of 265 CE-and as many other people have pointed out, there undoubtedly would be Romans involved, arguably enough to make it reasonable to question if there ever was a Roman Great Cult or if they had co-mingled enough with the proto-Diamond that you effectively just had the Awakened side of the Republic/Empire split between the proto-Diamond conglomerate and Roman Nameless Orders and Legacies. By the time Christianity was legalized and incorporated into the Roman Empire's state with the Edict of Milan in 313 CE, the Diamond had already had 48 years of being formally organized.<br /> <br /> Christianity, in the context of Awakening, is a religion born into a word where a faction is already in full swing archetypalizing national myth and belief and reaching for the root behind the symbols, and it's own factionalism through it's nascency pretty well means the religion just couldn't have the time build up enough unity to be a Great Cult before collision with the Diamond basically gave &quot;Christian&quot;(and I'll get to those quotations) mages a better option.<br /> <br /> And forget Islam. The Prophet Muhammad isn't even born until 570, and that's all smack dab in the heart of the Diamond Belt. The Diamond is not all that far off, temporally speaking, from the Tremere Adoption, so they are near the end of their struggling steps as being a unifying Middle Eastern Sect.<br /> <br /> And of course, both Christianity and Islam run into a handicap where they are distinctly <i>religious</i> structures rather than <i>spiritually national</i> structures. The faith and practices of the Great Cults before them were intertwined with their cultures so much as to be almost unquestionably inseparable, where Christianity and Islam still in a period of being <i>parallel</i> to their host nations, an outsider that needs to <i>integrated </i>into their adjacent surroundings, and that's disregarding the violence perpetrated against these cults through the period.<br /> <br /> Where that matter is that Awakening already does a lot to basically kill your faith-it's hard to believe a religion you grew up in when the light of Supernal Truth kind of shines a light for just how many, many holes are in the weave. The traditional Great Cults found their native myths and beliefs a fairly useful starting point, and the pantomiming of those practices had tangible benefits, and honestly the whole thing just very deeply rooted to a point where even if you don't believe a word of it, you still speak the religious and mythological language** but there was a reason the Diamond emerged from a truly world changing mass-integration of cultures rather than clutching their pearls against the blasphemies and heresies against their faith-it's a convienent language, but that Persian's stories fill the holes left in mine, and mine his, and when more and more mages combine their stories and understanding, the more Truth makes sense, and clinging to an absolute belief in your bedtime stories in that context is rather silly.<br /> <br /> Christians and Muslims, by contrast, do not grow up in a world where their version of their faith is literally spoken and portrayed all around them to a point of being background radiation, and so it's value to the individual is that much more contigent on being a hidden/argued truth(or put more simply, it <i>really</i> has to be true to be worth it) of the world that everyone else has to come around to....and then, upon Awakening, find themselves confronted with an even more hidden, more contentious, and far more substantively and objectively truthier truth of reality, all with a surprisingly large organization who can explain it and prove it way better than their forms of Christianity or Islam could.<br /> <br /> Yeah, there's no fucking way a Christian or an Islamic Great Cult ever happened. Surely you had cabals, Legacies, even Nameless Orders, because every mage has <i>some</i> Lie they believe in, but by the time either religion was substantial enough to have the same grounding effect Great Cult's mythos did, they'd be overshadowed by the Diamond and their nearest rising competitors, the religions already turned into tools as part of the arsenal of these entities.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Tremere emerged as the first major organization to come forward and be regarded as close to a peer to the Diamond at the time (coming to bargain from Scandinavia, central Europe, and India, no less) without so much as an attempt to articulate any Awakened attempt to unite under a Christian/Islamic identifying mass organization of any sort pretty well states it just wasn't happening, nevermind a Great Cult.<br /> <br /> As for the Nordic Great Cult....Did I mention that one of the directions the Tremere came from was Scandanavia? Yeah, think that answers that one, chief.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Granted, not fully incorporated, since the first thing the Consilium Age includes a mention that the Synhedrion didn't feel the need to fully integrate, but that's &quot;One God Above All Others&quot; monotheism for ya, baby.<br /> **For the same reason I don't believe in God but will still say &quot;Thank god&quot; or &quot;God damnit&quot; after being raised in a world where Christianity <i>is</i> intertwined with my culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T02:07:35-08:00","id":1545989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1545981#post1545981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Nordic Great Cult....Did I mention that one of the directions the Tremere came from was Scandanavia? Yeah, think that answers that one, chief.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really? Maybe I'm being stupid, but it seems to me you could draw a lot of different inferences from that fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T02:41:39-08:00","id":1545991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1545981#post1545981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Nordic Great Cult....Did I mention that one of the directions the Tremere came from was Scandanavia? Yeah, think that answers that one, chief.</div> </div> </div> </div>As <b>Micheal</b> pointed - no, Tremere are <b><i>not</i></b> Scandinavia Great Cult. Only one House of it - <b>Seo Hel</b> - comes from area, and Tremere literally hunt <i>Seo Hel</i> mages with other Scandinavian Awakened to incorporate this Legacy as House later on. Basically, original Seo Hel Legacy was to Scandinavian Great Cult what later be called 'Left-Handed' in Diamond.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nameless and Accursed p.140</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Her followers were outcasts, cursed and plagued by waking nightmares. These \u201cgrim-faced ones\u201d were considered too profane for poems and sagas, and even worse than the oft-denigrated <i>seith</i> followers of the Vanir, whose arts at least belonged to the world of life. The Norse of the time believed Hel\u2019s followers could prevent them from reaching Valhalla or Christian Heaven, for the goddess would claim anyone cursed by the Seo Hel Legacy, stripping their bones and nails to make the ships and weapons of Ragnar\u00f6k. Awakened Norse despised the soul-stealing sect on more refined grounds, but just as intensely. Thus, Sleepers and Awakened collaborated with the Tremere to destroy the Seo Hel.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-16-2024, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-16T10:36:24-08:00","id":1546002,"title":"","content":"I don't think there would have been a Nordic Great Cult that far back, because I think the inhabitants of that part of the world were not yet organised into states, and I think the level of social cohesion of a state is a requirement for the Awakened of that people to be organised to the level (and have the form of social interaction and integration) that makes them a Great Cult.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I think a key thing about the concept to be taken from To The Strongest is that I believe the Greek and Persian cults at the least are meant to be read as relatively recent formations. You had Greek mages who probably saw the Supernal through the lens of the common gods of the Greek tribes and cities before they started adopting the trappings and methods of philosophical schools, but I don't believe that the socially isolated mages viewed as somewhere between charlatans and lunatics could be called a Great Cult. Similar to how the Persian mages were more socially marginal before the gap created in the Zoroastrian priesthood by Alexander.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of the time, you get mages who exist in a social position resembling how they lived before the Sundering, apart and using their magic to help their communities, but removed from the context where a more accessible spirit world makes the need for them more apparent, Omphalos Stones allows some exposure without Quiescence, and there aren't shattered remains of the Time Before hanging around, they lose a lot of the prestige and support.<br /> <br /> If anything, the fact that the Tremere formed from many places that may not have had those support structures is even more impressive (but for the fact that the main uniting factor was realising the power that could be drawn from torturing monsters for Mysteries).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T02:44:12-08:00","id":1546120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1545981#post1545981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I can simplify the &quot;Christian Great Cult&quot; and &quot;Islamic Great Cult&quot; real nice and simple: there never would have been any; there would be, at best, Nameless Orders and Legacies.<br /> <br /> The Synhedrion aren't described in great detail in the Tome of the Pentacle, but between the fact that their one major entry implies that all theorizing about one Yeshua ben Yosef was provided to the Diamond by the Synhedrion and the way Dave frames it when he talks about them (I will namely highlight <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1511880-tome-of-the-pentacle-on-dtrpg?p=1513112#post1513112\">&quot;If every Great Cult provided something to the melting pot of the Diamond, their main contribution was a sense of responsibility.&quot;</a>), the Judean Great Cult was pretty well in the mix* by the time the Diamond officially forms by the Alexandrian Convocation of 265 CE-and as many other people have pointed out, there undoubtedly would be Romans involved, arguably enough to make it reasonable to question if there ever was a Roman Great Cult or if they had co-mingled enough with the proto-Diamond that you effectively just had the Awakened side of the Republic/Empire split between the proto-Diamond conglomerate and Roman Nameless Orders and Legacies. By the time Christianity was legalized and incorporated into the Roman Empire's state with the Edict of Milan in 313 CE, the Diamond had already had 48 years of being formally organized.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Synhedrion were...<br /> <br /> 1) Completely - and I mean completely - embedded into the Sleeper organisation of the same name.<br /> <br /> 2) Based on the contemporary-to-them <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merkabah_mysticism\" target=\"_blank\">Merkabah mysticism</a> rather than Kabala, as Kabala won't be invented for several centuries. The Synhedrion were scholars and rabbis who recorded, debated, and attempted to understand their Awakening visions and Mage Sight in the context of their religion, not Golem-creators.<br /> <br /> 3) Were the hardest of hardcore about magic only being the province of those wise enough to not misuse it.<br /> <br /> When we were writing Tome of the Pentacle, we had it in mind that <br /> <br /> a) Canonically, the Seers-to-be and Diamond-to-be at the time were two differences of opinion / political parties / arguments within the same organisation, named by later Diamond historians as the &quot;Tyrannic Antitype&quot; and &quot;Atlantean Antitype&quot;. The difference was, essentially, should mages rule Sleepers as an expression of the natural hierarchy of the worlds and their Awakened status, or should mages regard themselves as a people apart from Sleeping Empires and Nations, governing themselves? The Diamond Precept is &quot;The Awakened are one Nation&quot; - it's that declaration that expels the Exarchists into a millenium of Nameless Orders and eventually the Seers, and makes the Five Diamond Orders out of their Darshanas.<br /> <br /> b) We (by which I mean I) do not believe in bloodless revolutions and clean transitions. Every great change in the makeup of the setting should have refuseniks and outliers. I wanted to show a Great Cult that *didn't* go into the Diamond, but was a peer and influenced some of its thinking. The Synhedrion would fit - it's the Hellenic culture that got left out of To The Strongest for space.<br /> <br /> c) The conflict between the antitypes is all well and theoretical, but the proto-Seers would have had to do something to get Unnamed by the rest of the Awakened community. First edition presented Diamond mages in the Roman Empire as being fringe thinkers and Greek imports, with power in the Empire held by Seers (conflicting with the fact that Seers shouldn't exist yet) - especially the Praetorian Ministry, or their ancestors anyway.<br /> <br /> d) Seers of the Throne sure do have a lot of Jewish terms in their lexicon. Why the fuck is a Profane Urim called that?<br /> <br /> e) While we're on the subject, there's an inherent conflict between a Synhedrion that tries to interpret the mind of God from their visions while remaining morally-centered and, well... How Prelacies work for Seers. Interpreting what you see in Mage Sight to determine the wishes of the divine is what a Prelate does, for certain values of &quot;the Divine&quot;, and that's probably why the Synhedrion are so careful with their practices. They're competition to the Tyrannics, who won't worship the Iron Seals like they &quot;should&quot;.<br /> <br /> f) So if we take that forward and adapt it to second edition, we have Tyrannic-minded mages buying into the Empire, a Great Cult tied to a culture that's about to get horribly persecuted by that Empire, our desire for a Cult that stays &quot;outside&quot;, our need for Tyrannic mages to do something terrible in the eyes of their Atlantean peers, parallel or conflicting practices between the Cult and the basic Sight&gt;Prelate loop of a Seer, modern Seers of the Throne who mock that Cult's religion with their terms for things...<br /> <br /> ... It all adds up to &quot;things do not end well for the Synhedrion&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which is why the final chapter glosses over them. It's both too complicated and if handled poorly full of potential antisemitic pittraps. Somewhere out there is a rpg freelancer who's versed in Merkabah enough to write intelligently about it (and is willing to do so despite it being a closed practice maybe not suitable for turning into a game for outsiders) and depict the effect the first Jewish-Roman war and the destruction of the second temple had on them.<br /> <br /> But that freelancer is <u>not me</u>.<br /> <br /> As it stands in the gameline, the Synhedrion's fate is mysterious. Maybe they did join into the Diamond. Maybe the final straw for the Diamond kicking the Prelates out came later, or had a different cause. Maybe we don't have to have yet another Jewish faction of mages in a roleplaying game murdered to make a point. We don't really use the appropriated terms for Seer artifacts any more (notice how the line tries to say &quot;Profane Robe&quot; most of the time) and they have a perfectly good explanation even if they do stay - Paternoster, when it first started up over a millenium later, looted a *lot* of things. Including the Teraphim, which is one of the items in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T02:54:12-08:00","id":1546121,"title":"","content":"As for Muslims... It is hinted as much as is possible without confirming something that should not be confirmed that the Corpus Author was a Muslim woman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T09:53:32-08:00","id":1546133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1546120#post1546120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Synhedrion were...<br /> <br /> 1) Completely - and I mean completely - embedded into the Sleeper organisation of the same name.<br /> <br /> 2) Based on the contemporary-to-them <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merkabah_mysticism\" target=\"_blank\">Merkabah mysticism</a> rather than Kabala, as Kabala won't be invented for several centuries. The Synhedrion were scholars and rabbis who recorded, debated, and attempted to understand their Awakening visions and Mage Sight in the context of their religion, not Golem-creators.<br /> <br /> 3) Were the hardest of hardcore about magic only being the province of those wise enough to not misuse it.<br /> <br /> When we were writing Tome of the Pentacle, we had it in mind that<br /> <br /> a) Canonically, the Seers-to-be and Diamond-to-be at the time were two differences of opinion / political parties / arguments within the same organisation, named by later Diamond historians as the &quot;Tyrannic Antitype&quot; and &quot;Atlantean Antitype&quot;. The difference was, essentially, should mages rule Sleepers as an expression of the natural hierarchy of the worlds and their Awakened status, or should mages regard themselves as a people apart from Sleeping Empires and Nations, governing themselves? The Diamond Precept is &quot;The Awakened are one Nation&quot; - it's that declaration that expels the Exarchists into a millenium of Nameless Orders and eventually the Seers, and makes the Five Diamond Orders out of their Darshanas.<br /> <br /> b) We (by which I mean I) do not believe in bloodless revolutions and clean transitions. Every great change in the makeup of the setting should have refuseniks and outliers. I wanted to show a Great Cult that *didn't* go into the Diamond, but was a peer and influenced some of its thinking. The Synhedrion would fit - it's the Hellenic culture that got left out of To The Strongest for space.<br /> <br /> c) The conflict between the antitypes is all well and theoretical, but the proto-Seers would have had to do something to get Unnamed by the rest of the Awakened community. First edition presented Diamond mages in the Roman Empire as being fringe thinkers and Greek imports, with power in the Empire held by Seers (conflicting with the fact that Seers shouldn't exist yet) - especially the Praetorian Ministry, or their ancestors anyway.<br /> <br /> d) Seers of the Throne sure do have a lot of Jewish terms in their lexicon. Why the fuck is a Profane Urim called that?<br /> <br /> e) While we're on the subject, there's an inherent conflict between a Synhedrion that tries to interpret the mind of God from their visions while remaining morally-centered and, well... How Prelacies work for Seers. Interpreting what you see in Mage Sight to determine the wishes of the divine is what a Prelate does, for certain values of &quot;the Divine&quot;, and that's probably why the Synhedrion are so careful with their practices. They're competition to the Tyrannics, who won't worship the Iron Seals like they &quot;should&quot;.<br /> <br /> f) So if we take that forward and adapt it to second edition, we have Tyrannic-minded mages buying into the Empire, a Great Cult tied to a culture that's about to get horribly persecuted by that Empire, our desire for a Cult that stays &quot;outside&quot;, our need for Tyrannic mages to do something terrible in the eyes of their Atlantean peers, parallel or conflicting practices between the Cult and the basic Sight&gt;Prelate loop of a Seer, modern Seers of the Throne who mock that Cult's religion with their terms for things...<br /> <br /> ... It all adds up to &quot;things do not end well for the Synhedrion&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Which is why the final chapter glosses over them. It's both too complicated and if handled poorly full of potential antisemitic pittraps. Somewhere out there is a rpg freelancer who's versed in Merkabah enough to write intelligently about it (and is willing to do so despite it being a closed practice maybe not suitable for turning into a game for outsiders) and depict the effect the first Jewish-Roman war and the destruction of the second temple had on them.<br /> <br /> But that freelancer is <u>not me</u>.<br /> <br /> As it stands in the gameline, the Synhedrion's fate is mysterious. Maybe they did join into the Diamond. Maybe the final straw for the Diamond kicking the Prelates out came later, or had a different cause. Maybe we don't have to have yet another Jewish faction of mages in a roleplaying game murdered to make a point. We don't really use the appropriated terms for Seer artifacts any more (notice how the line tries to say &quot;Profane Robe&quot; most of the time) and they have a perfectly good explanation even if they do stay - Paternoster, when it first started up over a millenium later, looted a *lot* of things. Including the Teraphim, which is one of the items in question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that clarifies that. I stand corrected and edified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T11:54:36-08:00","id":1546145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1546133#post1546133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that clarifies that. I stand corrected and edified.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, while we're talking Inside Baseball, the reason for &quot;antitype&quot; is that I really, really wanted to call the proto-Diamond &quot;The Atlantean Paradigm&quot; in order to fuck with people, but Paradigm is a wholly inappropriate word for neoplatonists of the time, while Antitype is something they would have maybe called themselves. The sacrifices we make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-20T01:23:30-08:00","id":1546183,"title":"","content":"Circling back to my original bit, I will take a second to note that I avoided leaning into what the Tyrannic Antitype* might have done with a nascent growth of Awakened Christians and Muslims because...well, I imagine in you're faithful but also into this game, having someone on the internet point out incorporation into that Antitype is the real trajectory that would devour any would be Great Cult isn't fun.<br /> <br /> But, like, there's the other real answer.<br /> <br /> *glad to remember we have those terms now that it's come up<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-20T05:11:41-08:00","id":1546187,"title":"","content":"Yeah. So. The &quot;missing&quot; powerblock of Christian mages isn't missing at all. It's called The Keepers of the Word. And then, after the newborn Mysterium abandons it as territory, Paternoster takes it over.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T10:10:37-08:00","id":1546248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1546121#post1546121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Muslims... It is hinted as much as is possible without confirming something that should not be confirmed that the Corpus Author was a Muslim woman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a reason for this, something about Islamic theology that made it makes sense, or culture, or did it just feel right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T12:10:23-08:00","id":1546251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1546248#post1546248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there a reason for this, something about Islamic theology that made it makes sense, or culture, or did it just feel right?</div> </div> </div> </div>The best mage-related game of any of the three (Ars, Ascension, Awakening) I have ever been even tangentially involved with was a Dark Ages: Mage game set in Andaluc\u00eda. That's what I was thinking when I turned her from a mystery to a character in Imperial Mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-21T12:49:07-08:00","id":1546253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1546183#post1546183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Circling back to my original bit, I will take a second to note that I avoided leaning into what the Tyrannic Antitype* might have done with a nascent growth of Awakened Christians and Muslims because...well, I imagine in you're faithful but also into this game, having someone on the internet point out incorporation into that Antitype is the real trajectory that would devour any would be Great Cult isn't fun.<br /> <br /> But, like, there's the other real answer.<br /> <br /> *glad to remember we have those terms now that it's come up</div> </div> </div> </div>As a faithful Christian who is into this game, I'm not at all offended by speculations on the history of Christianity as presented within the fiction of the game.<br /> <br /> The bits about the Synhedrion are interesting as someone who is interested in RL early Judaism. I have an NPC who is a high attainment Eyes of Ain Soph mage who will soon be taking the stage in the chronicle I'm storytelling. It would be interesting to think about how Kaballah formed within the context of Awakened history.<br /> <br /> Chinese culture is also an important part of the chronicle. Any thoughts on Chinese great cults?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27436-calvinsiler","name":"CalvinSiler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27436_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-23T04:28:34-08:00","id":1546300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1545812#post1545812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rough draft for <b>Awakened Christianity</b> - for my Rome games. ( It's very important for Rome Empire in 2nd till 5th century AD - and probably from there on. ) Probably similar would work probably for Judaism and Islam versions of it.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Awakened Christianity</i></b><br /> <br /> <b>What is magic? </b>Magic is boon send from God and their angels.<br /> <br /> <b>What is Fallen World? </b>World was created perfect by God. With Atlantean fall of Towers to Heaven - God cursed whole creation to become Fallen World as it is.<br /> <br /> <b>Who are Exarchs and Oracles? </b>Exarch AND Oracles are both emanations of One True God. Many times they are called as Archangels on particular Path.<br /> <br /> <b>What is High Speech</b>? High Speech is language of Angels - later known as <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enochian\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Enochian</b></a><br /> <br /> <b>What is Abyss</b>? Absence of the divine light, pointed to the theology of St Augustine of Hippo. Some intellectual in Awakened Christianity posits it's parts of Creation rejected by God. In later centuries other posits it's literal Hell, or spread of Hell, directly from the Devil.<br /> <br /> <b>What is Supernal Realms? </b>Supernal Realms are higher planes, outside of normal reality, each governed by one Archangel. They are still only 'filters' of One True Higher reality, ruled all at once, by God themselves.<br /> <br /> <b>Aether</b> - Havens of All Mighty, under <b><i>Archangel Micheal</i></b><br /> <b>Arcadia</b> - Under guidance of <i><b>Gabriel</b></i>, past World BEFORE Creation of Humans - perfect, but also somehow pagan.<br /> <b>Pandemonium</b> - Purgatory, ruled by the angel of judgment <i><b>Phanuel</b></i>. ( In Middle Ages, it's changed into literal 'Hell of sinners, ruled by <i><b>Lucifer</b></i>' )<br /> <b>Primal Wild </b>- Garden of Eden AFTER creation of Adam and Eve, especially with Tree of Knowledge, under guidance of <i><b>Rafael</b></i><br /> <b>Stygia</b> - Mausoleums and Cathedrals of previous dead, under watch of <b><i>Uriel </i></b>( See <a href=\"https://www.angelarium.net/seraphim#/the-driftwood-cathedral/\" target=\"_blank\">Driftwood Cathedral</a> for inspiration )<br /> <br /> <b>What are local Darshanas (proto-Orders)?</b><br /> Christianity was created just AFTER first integration of Atlantean Orders in Ancient Rome, circa 1st century BCE. ( With Christianity creation on whole 1st century AD. ) It's widespread of this religion in Mediterranean Sea area is joined with creation Diamond as organisations Alliance. All of Darshanas of it ARE Atlantean and Seers Orders - even in modern times, it's rather minority percentage but still sustained in general multicultural tapestry of Diamond Cults beliefs systems, when more and more Awakened eshew more religious roots of their magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am confused, shouldn't Arcadia and Primal Wild be switched conceptually? The Primal Wild is the world without humans as far as I understand, and Arcadia's fae clearly have human influence or some human-like seeming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T09:56:28-08:00","id":1546343,"title":"","content":"I don't really see the Garden of Eden matching very well to the vibe of the Thyrsus Path and the vision of the Supernal it sees. At most, I could see that as a motif they reference for the idea of humanity closer to a state of nature, but even that is probably extrapolating from scriptural narrative rather than referencing it directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1546300#post1546300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Primal Wild is the world without humans as far as I understand</div> </div> </div> </div>To the extent that the Supernal Realms should be regarded in terms of being literal, coherent places, the Primal Wild is not nature as it would be without human intervention, it's something representative of the idea that all living things are interconnected (including the idea that everything that seems whole is itself built out of smaller organisms), that all actions are consequential (and those consequences endure and perpetuate themselves), and the visceral, ecstatic sensation of drifting through these bonds. It's not a world without humanity, it's humanity as inextricably part of the world.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-01T14:07:21-08:00","id":1546520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1546120#post1546120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">e) While we're on the subject, there's an inherent conflict between a Synhedrion that tries to interpret the mind of God from their visions while remaining morally-centered and, well... How Prelacies work for Seers. Interpreting what you see in Mage Sight to determine the wishes of the divine is what a Prelate does, for certain values of &quot;the Divine&quot;, and that's probably why the Synhedrion are so careful with their practices. They're competition to the Tyrannics, who won't worship the Iron Seals like they &quot;should&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weather or not they're decedents from the Synhedrion or Jewish, the idea of a modern era Nameless Order that has Prelates but worships something benevolent is actually a really cool concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-01T18:54:24-08:00","id":1546524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1546520#post1546520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Weather or not they're decedents from the Synhedrion or Jewish, the idea of a modern era Nameless Order that has Prelates but worships something benevolent is actually a really cool concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Prelates as in the same Merit that grants Seers the Mystery Commands Condition?<br /> <br /> Is this an idea of something other than the Exarchs putting its hooks into a mage's soul like that (which the Exarchs tolerate for some reason) or somebody with an existing Prelacy who manages to really convince themselves that the Mystery Commands they receive mean something other than what they seem?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T02:44:58-08:00","id":1546531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1546520#post1546520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weather or not they're decedents from the Synhedrion or Jewish, the idea of a modern era Nameless Order that has Prelates but worships something benevolent is actually a really cool concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me it would feel a bit weird. Like, a big draw to the Exarchs is that they're the only game in town. If you want to meet the divine and have that divine power talk back, then you're going to have to make do with a bunch of evil tyrants. The benevolent divine, if it exists, doesn't talk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T03:49:40-08:00","id":1546682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1546531#post1546531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me it would feel a bit weird. Like, a big draw to the Exarchs is that they're the only game in town. If you want to meet the divine and have that divine power talk back, then you're going to have to make do with a bunch of evil tyrants. The benevolent divine, if it exists, doesn't talk.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Mage is a horror setting. God exists, but he's The Father.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-06T07:12:44-08:00","id":1546688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545774-mtaw-dark-eras-fan-created-great-cults?p=1546531#post1546531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me it would 